IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g5-interpretation`
IMPORT `g5-nouns`
IMPORT `g5-art13-effects`
IMPORT `g5-art13-reporting`
IMPORT `g5-art14-court-powers`
IMPORT `ind-b-tests-fixtures-g5`

-- ind-b-tests-art13-14: independent tests of Articles 13 and 14 (group G5), by test author ind-b.
-- Every expected value comes from work/ind-b/expectations.md, written from the Law before this module's imports were opened; each assertion cites its row id.
-- A section headed "reading checks" tests a non-default reading of a fork against what that reading itself says; its expected values are not rows of expectations.md.

§ `Article 13(1) -- while registered (rows E13-01 to E13-05)`

-- E13-01: registered in the general section: (2) to (4) apply.
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 a general-section company charity` `ind-b5 today`
-- E13-02: registered in the restricted section: they apply.
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 a restricted-section company charity` `ind-b5 today`
-- E13-03: deregistered: they no longer apply.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 a company charity deregistered on 1 January 2024` `ind-b5 today`
-- E13-04: no longer meets the charity test but not deregistered: they still apply (the rule has no input for the test: only deregistration ends them).
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 a general-section company charity` (YMD 2026 1 1)
-- E13-05: before registration (an applicant): they do not apply.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 a general-section company charity` (YMD 2019 1 9)

§ `Article 13(2), (3) and (13) -- amending the purposes (rows E13-06 to E13-16)`

-- E13-06: a power to amend the purposes to include a non-charitable purpose is of no effect.
#ASSERT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 a general-section company charity` `ind-b5 today` (`ind-b5 provision permitting` (LIST `ind-b5 a non-charitable purpose`) FALSE)
-- E13-07: a power to add a different charitable purpose is not struck by 13(2); 13(3) governs it.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 a general-section company charity` `ind-b5 today` (`ind-b5 provision permitting` (LIST `ind-b5 a charitable purpose`) FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) paragraph (3) applies to the provision` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 a general-section company charity` `ind-b5 today` (`ind-b5 provision permitting` (LIST `ind-b5 a charitable purpose`) FALSE)
-- E13-08: deregistered: 13(2) does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 a company charity deregistered on 1 January 2024` `ind-b5 today` (`ind-b5 provision permitting` (LIST `ind-b5 a non-charitable purpose`) FALSE)
-- E13-09 and E13-12: evidence to the Commissioner's satisfaction and prior approval: the amendment (adding or substituting) is open.
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) the amendment of purposes is subject to evidence and approval` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 a general-section company charity` `ind-b5 today` (`ind-b5 provision permitting` (LIST `ind-b5 a charitable purpose`) FALSE) TRUE TRUE
-- E13-10: no prior approval: not open.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(3) the amendment of purposes is subject to evidence and approval` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 a general-section company charity` `ind-b5 today` (`ind-b5 provision permitting` (LIST `ind-b5 a charitable purpose`) FALSE) TRUE FALSE
-- E13-11: approval but no evidence: not open.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(3) the amendment of purposes is subject to evidence and approval` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 a general-section company charity` `ind-b5 today` (`ind-b5 provision permitting` (LIST `ind-b5 a charitable purpose`) FALSE) FALSE TRUE
-- E13-13: an 1862 association, a Loi of 1862 order inconsistent with 13(3), no approval: 13(3) yields, the amendment is open.
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) the amendment of purposes is subject to evidence and approval` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 an 1862 association charity` `ind-b5 today` (`ind-b5 provision permitting` (LIST `ind-b5 a charitable purpose`) TRUE) FALSE FALSE
-- E13-14: a fideicommis, a Loi of 1862 order (made before registration) inconsistent with 13(2): 13(2) does not strike the provision.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 a fideicommis charity` `ind-b5 today` (`ind-b5 provision permitting` (LIST `ind-b5 a non-charitable purpose`) TRUE)
#ASSERT `Art 13(13) paragraphs (2) and (3) yield to an order under the Loi of 1862` `ind-b5 a fideicommis charity` (`ind-b5 provision permitting` (LIST `ind-b5 a non-charitable purpose`) TRUE)
-- E13-15: a company: 13(13) does not reach it; 13(3) applies.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(13) paragraphs (2) and (3) yield to an order under the Loi of 1862` `ind-b5 a general-section company charity` (`ind-b5 provision permitting` (LIST `ind-b5 a charitable purpose`) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(3) the amendment of purposes is subject to evidence and approval` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 a general-section company charity` `ind-b5 today` (`ind-b5 provision permitting` (LIST `ind-b5 a charitable purpose`) TRUE) FALSE FALSE
-- E13-16: an 1862 association with no order: 13(3) applies in full.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(3) the amendment of purposes is subject to evidence and approval` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 an 1862 association charity` `ind-b5 today` (`ind-b5 provision permitting` (LIST `ind-b5 a charitable purpose`) FALSE) FALSE FALSE

§ `Article 13(4) and (5) (rows E13-17 to E13-24)`

-- E13-17: the duty to provide public benefit per the statement is the registered charity's, and stands while registered.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (`Art 13(4) the registered charity must provide public benefit in accordance with its statement` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 a general-section company charity` `ind-b5 today` FALSE)
#ASSERT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (`Art 13(4) the registered charity must provide public benefit in accordance with its statement` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 a company charity deregistered on 1 January 2024` `ind-b5 today` FALSE)
-- E13-18: asking approval of a statement amendment without satisfying evidence does not discharge the 13(4)(b) duty; with it, it does.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 13(4)(b) the registered charity that requests approval of an amendment of its statement must provide evidence` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 a general-section company charity` `ind-b5 today` TRUE FALSE) 0 (LIST EVENT `a registered charity` `provide evidence of a reason justifying the request, to the satisfaction of the Commissioner` 1))
#ASSERT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 13(4)(b) the registered charity that requests approval of an amendment of its statement must provide evidence` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 a general-section company charity` `ind-b5 today` TRUE TRUE) 0 (LIST EVENT `a registered charity` `provide evidence of a reason justifying the request, to the satisfaction of the Commissioner` 1))
-- E13-19: meets the original condition: complies.
#ASSERT `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section meets what paragraph (5) requires` `ind-b5 A` (`ind-b5 restricted facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- E13-20: ceased; prior permission given before it ceased; meets the different condition: complies.
#ASSERT `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section meets what paragraph (5) requires` `ind-b5 A` (`ind-b5 restricted facts` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- E13-21: permission only after it ceased: contravenes.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section meets what paragraph (5) requires` `ind-b5 A` (`ind-b5 restricted facts` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- E13-22: meets neither: contravenes.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section meets what paragraph (5) requires` `ind-b5 A` (`ind-b5 restricted facts` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- E13-23: a general-section charity: no 13(5) duty.
#ASSERT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (`Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section must ensure it meets its condition` `ind-b5 A` TRUE `ind-b5 a general-section company charity` (`ind-b5 restricted facts` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (`Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section must ensure it meets its condition` `ind-b5 A` TRUE `ind-b5 a restricted-section company charity` (`ind-b5 restricted facts` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- E13-24: a prior permission for a different condition it does not meet, while it still meets the original: complies, by (a).
#ASSERT `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section meets what paragraph (5) requires` `ind-b5 A` (`ind-b5 restricted facts` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§ `Article 13(6) -- what must be reported (rows E13-25 to E13-36)`

-- E13-25 (a): a change in a matter entered on the register.
#ASSERT `ind-b5 a general charity must report` (`a change in a matter about which information is entered on the register` TRUE TRUE)
-- E13-26 (b): a matter coming to light after registration that could have led to refusal.
#ASSERT `ind-b5 a general charity must report` (`a matter coming to light after registration or after permission for a change of name` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- E13-27 (c): a proposal to change the constitution.
#ASSERT `ind-b5 a general charity must report` (`a proposal to change the charity's constitution` TRUE)
-- E13-28 (d): a proposal that could result in the charity ceasing to meet 11(4)(c) or (d).
#ASSERT `ind-b5 a general charity must report` (`a proposal or an event affecting the requirements of Article 11(4)(c) or (d)` TRUE FALSE)
-- E13-29 (e): a governor's reportable matter the charity knows was not reported.
#ASSERT `ind-b5 a general charity must report` (`a reportable matter in relation to a governor` "G. Brown" TRUE)
-- E13-30 (e): the charity does not know the governor failed to report: not under (e).
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b5 a general charity must report` (`a reportable matter in relation to a governor` "G. Brown" FALSE)
-- E13-31 (f): a matter likely to lead to winding up.
#ASSERT `ind-b5 a general charity must report` (`a matter likely to lead to bankruptcy, winding up or ceasing to exist` TRUE)
-- E13-32 (g): restricted section, a proposal to change how it meets its condition.
#ASSERT `ind-b5 a restricted charity must report` (`a proposal to change how or whether the charity meets its restricted-section condition` TRUE)
-- E13-33 (g): a general-section charity, same proposal: not under (g).
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b5 a general charity must report` (`a proposal to change how or whether the charity meets its restricted-section condition` TRUE)
-- E13-34 (h): a prescribed matter.
#ASSERT `ind-b5 a general charity must report` (`a matter prescribed by Order under Article 13(6)(h)` TRUE)
-- E13-35: a change of something not on the register and not prescribed: no 13(6) duty.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b5 a general charity must report` (`a change in a matter about which information is entered on the register` FALSE TRUE)
-- E13-36: the duty is the registered charity's; its prompt report discharges it.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (`Art 13(6) the registered charity must promptly report the matter` `ind-b5 A` TRUE `ind-b5 a general-section company charity` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`a proposal to change the charity's constitution` TRUE) `ind-b5 timing` `ind-b5 a prompt report`)
#ASSERT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 13(6) the registered charity must promptly report the matter` `ind-b5 A` TRUE `ind-b5 a general-section company charity` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`a proposal to change the charity's constitution` TRUE) `ind-b5 timing` `ind-b5 a prompt report`) 0 (LIST EVENT `a registered charity` (`report a matter to the Commissioner` (`a proposal to change the charity's constitution` TRUE)) 1))
-- E13-36: an entity that is not a registered charity owes no 13(6) report.
#ASSERT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (`Art 13(6) the registered charity must promptly report the matter` `ind-b5 A` FALSE `ind-b5 a general-section company charity` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`a proposal to change the charity's constitution` TRUE) `ind-b5 timing` `ind-b5 a prompt report`)

§ `Article 13(7) to (12) (rows E13-37 to E13-48)`

-- E13-37: the registered charity must send an annual return; sending discharges it.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (`Art 13(7) the registered charity must send an annual return` `ind-b5 A` TRUE (`Order under Article 13(7) and (8)` OF NOTHING, NOTHING))
#ASSERT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 13(7) the registered charity must send an annual return` `ind-b5 A` TRUE (`Order under Article 13(7) and (8)` OF NOTHING, NOTHING)) 0 (LIST EVENT `a registered charity` `send the annual return to the Commissioner` 1))
-- E13-38: 13(8) lets an Order under 13(7) deal with format and timing, lateness and register entries.
#ASSERT `Art 13(8) paragraph (8) lets an Order under paragraph (7) cover the subject` `the format and timing of the annual return, Article 13(8)`
#ASSERT `Art 13(8) paragraph (8) lets an Order under paragraph (7) cover the subject` `the consequences of lateness of the annual return, Article 13(8)`
#ASSERT `Art 13(8) paragraph (8) lets an Order under paragraph (7) cover the subject` `the entries to be made on the register in respect of the annual return, Article 13(8)`
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (`Art 13(8) the Minister may by Order provide for the format and timing of the annual return` `the format and timing of the annual return, Article 13(8)` TRUE)
-- E13-39: the Minister's 13(9) powers.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` `Art 13(9)(a) the Minister may by Order require payment details in the annual return`
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` `Art 13(9)(b) the Minister may by Order require a statement of intentions`
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` `Art 13(9)(c) the Minister may by Order provide for entry on the register`
#ASSERT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE `Art 13(9)(a) the Minister may by Order require payment details in the annual return` 0 (LIST EVENT `the Minister` (`make an Order` `the details of payments to a governor that an annual return must include, Article 13(9)(a)`) 1))
-- E13-40: relief Order after consulting the Commissioner AND a representative body: within the power.
#ASSERT `Art 13(10) the Minister may by Order provide the relief` (`ind-b5 relief order` TRUE TRUE `a provision of paragraph (6)`)
-- E13-41: the Commissioner not consulted: outside.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(10) the Minister may by Order provide the relief` (`ind-b5 relief order` FALSE TRUE `a provision of paragraph (6)`)
-- E13-42: no representative body consulted: outside.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(10) the Minister may by Order provide the relief` (`ind-b5 relief order` TRUE FALSE `a provision of paragraph (6)`)
-- E13-41 as effect: an Order made without the consultations leaves the provision applying in full.
#ASSERT `Art 13(10) the effect of the relief Order on the provision` `ind-b5 A` (`ind-b5 relief order` FALSE TRUE `a provision of paragraph (6)`) `a provision of paragraph (6)` EQUALS `the provision applies in full`
-- E13-44: a valid relief Order disapplying an Order under (9): the provision does not apply to the charity.
#ASSERT `Art 13(10) the effect of the relief Order on the provision` `ind-b5 A` (`ind-b5 relief order` TRUE TRUE `a provision of an Order under paragraph (9)`) `a provision of an Order under paragraph (9)` EQUALS `the provision does not apply to the charity`
-- E13-45: a payment inconsistent with the 13(9)(b) statement: contravenes; the prohibition binds a registered charity to which a 13(9) Order applies.
#ASSERT `Art 13(11)(a) the payment is inconsistent with the statement` `ind-b5 A` (`ind-b5 a payment` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (`Art 13(11)(a) the registered charity must not make a payment inconsistent with its statement` `ind-b5 A` TRUE TRUE)
-- E13-46: a consistent payment: no contravention.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(11)(a) the payment is inconsistent with the statement` `ind-b5 A` (`ind-b5 a payment` FALSE)
-- E13-47: the charity MAY apply, with reasons, to amend the statement; an application with reasons exercises it.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (`Art 13(11)(b) the registered charity may apply for permission to amend the statement` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 13(11)(b) the registered charity may apply for permission to amend the statement` TRUE TRUE) 0 (LIST EVENT `a registered charity` (`apply to the Commissioner for permission to amend the statement of intentions` "our plans have changed") 1))
-- E13-48: the States' 13(12) power, in Regulations under 11(7).
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (`Art 13(12) the States may require a charity to avoid or report and remedy a later ground for refusal` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Art 13(12) the situation is one the Regulations may require the charity or its governors to avoid or to report and remedy` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(12) the situation is one the Regulations may require the charity or its governors to avoid or to report and remedy` FALSE TRUE

§ `Article 14 -- the court's powers (rows E14-01 to E14-20)`

-- E14-01: Commissioner's application, misconduct in the administration: the powers are exercisable.
#ASSERT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `ind-b5 A` TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` TRUE (`ind-b5 appears` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- E14-02: AG's application, necessary to protect the property: exercisable.
#ASSERT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `ind-b5 A` TRUE `an application by the Attorney General` FALSE (`ind-b5 appears` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- E14-03: neither ground: not exercisable.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `ind-b5 A` TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` FALSE (`ind-b5 appears` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- E14-04: an application by a governor (anyone else) or by the charity itself: not exercisable under 14(1).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `ind-b5 A` TRUE `an application by any other person` TRUE (`ind-b5 appears` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `ind-b5 A` TRUE `an application by the registered charity` TRUE (`ind-b5 appears` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- E14-06: the entity is not a registered charity: not exercisable.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `ind-b5 A` FALSE `an application by the Commissioner` TRUE (`ind-b5 appears` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- E14-01 as a rule: the Commissioner may apply, and the court may then exercise the powers.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (`Art 14(1) the court may exercise the powers on the application` `ind-b5 A` TRUE TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` TRUE (`ind-b5 appears` TRUE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (`Art 14(1) the court may exercise the powers on the application` `ind-b5 A` TRUE TRUE `an application by any other person` TRUE (`ind-b5 appears` TRUE TRUE FALSE))
-- E14-08 to E14-16: each kind of order of 14(3), directed as the paragraph says, is one the court may make.
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` (`ind-b5 order` `an order prohibiting the charity or a governor from holding out as a charity, soliciting donations or another specified action` `a governor of the charity` (JUST `referring to or holding out the entity as a charity or Jersey charity, or as being charitable, having charitable purposes or providing public benefit`) FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` (`ind-b5 order` `an order prohibiting the charity or a governor from holding out as a charity, soliciting donations or another specified action` `the charity` (JUST `soliciting donations from the public, as specified in the order`) FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` (`ind-b5 order` `an order appointing a person to manage the affairs of the charity in place of its governors` `no person in particular` NOTHING FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` (`ind-b5 order` `an order appointing a person to be a governor` `no person in particular` NOTHING FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` (`ind-b5 order` `an order suspending or removing a governor or another person concerned in the management` `a governor of the charity` NOTHING FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` (`ind-b5 order` `an order suspending or removing a governor or another person concerned in the management` `another person concerned in the management or control of the charity` NOTHING FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` (`ind-b5 order` `an order requiring a holder of property not to part with it without the court's consent` `a person who holds property on behalf of the charity` NOTHING FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` (`ind-b5 order` `an order restricting transactions or payments without the court's consent` `the charity` NOTHING FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` (`ind-b5 order` `an order subjecting the administration to supervision, restraint or conditions` `the charity` NOTHING FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` (`ind-b5 order` `an order requiring a person to take steps to remedy the effects of misconduct` `a governor of the charity` NOTHING TRUE)
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is of a kind the paragraph lists` (`ind-b5 order` `an order making ancillary provision` `no person in particular` NOTHING FALSE)
-- E14-08 to E14-16 as a rule: once 14(1) is met the court may make the order.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (`Art 14(3) the court may make the order` `ind-b5 A` TRUE `an application by the Attorney General` TRUE (`ind-b5 appears` TRUE TRUE FALSE) (`ind-b5 order` `an order appointing a person to be a governor` `no person in particular` NOTHING FALSE))
-- E14-17: amend or revoke on the application of the Commissioner, the AG, the charity, or a person the order was directed to.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (`Art 14(4) the court may amend or revoke an order` TRUE TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (`Art 14(4) the court may amend or revoke an order` TRUE TRUE `an application by the Attorney General` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (`Art 14(4) the court may amend or revoke an order` TRUE TRUE `an application by the registered charity` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (`Art 14(4) the court may amend or revoke an order` TRUE TRUE `an application by a person to whom the order was directed` TRUE)
-- E14-18: an unrelated person, or a governor the order was not directed to: no 14(4) standing.
#ASSERT `ind-b5 nothing is owed under` (`Art 14(4) the court may amend or revoke an order` TRUE TRUE `an application by any other person` TRUE)
-- E14-19: a constitution that forbids the order does not take the power away.
#ASSERT `Art 14(5) the powers apply in addition to other powers and despite the constitution` TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- E14-20: the Commissioner's own power is unaffected by a pending application.
#ASSERT `Art 14(6) the Commissioner's own power is unaffected by the powers of the court` TRUE TRUE

§ `Reading checks for G5 (expected values from each reading's own words)`

-- F5.8 B (a prior permission replaces the original condition): the E13-24 charity, which does not meet the different condition, fails on that reading.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section meets what paragraph (5) requires` `the interpretation with the permission replacing the condition` (`ind-b5 restricted facts` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- F5.7 B (only a purpose neither charitable nor ancillary is caught): a power to add a purely ancillary purpose is not struck on that reading.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `the interpretation with ancillary purposes not caught` `ind-b5 a general-section company charity` `ind-b5 today` (`ind-b5 provision permitting` (LIST (Purpose WITH description IS "fundraising", head IS NOTHING, `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS TRUE, `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS FALSE, `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS FALSE)) FALSE)
-- F5.7 A (taken): the same power IS struck (a purely ancillary purpose is not a charitable purpose).
#ASSERT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 a general-section company charity` `ind-b5 today` (`ind-b5 provision permitting` (LIST (Purpose WITH description IS "fundraising", head IS NOTHING, `is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose of the entity` IS TRUE, `is advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election` IS FALSE, `is advancing a philosophical belief` IS FALSE)) FALSE)
-- F5.6 B (the effective day of deregistration still a day of registration).
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` `the interpretation with the effective day inside the registration` `ind-b5 a company charity deregistered on 1 January 2024` (YMD 2024 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 a company charity deregistered on 1 January 2024` (YMD 2024 1 1)
-- F5.4 B (any misconduct within 2(10)) and C (misconduct in the ordinary sense).
#ASSERT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `the interpretation with any misconduct` TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` TRUE (`ind-b5 appears` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `ind-b5 A` TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` TRUE (`ind-b5 appears` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Art 14(1) the powers of the court are exercisable on the application` `the interpretation with misconduct in the ordinary sense` TRUE `an application by the Commissioner` FALSE (`ind-b5 appears` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- F5.12 B (an order must serve all three purposes of 14(2)).
#ASSERT `Art 14(2) the order is one the court sees fit` `ind-b5 A` (`Order that the court sees fit under Article 14(2)` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(2) the order is one the court sees fit` `the interpretation with all three purposes` (`Order that the court sees fit under Article 14(2)` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE)
-- F5.14 B (any statement provided): a payment inconsistent only with an earlier, superseded statement.
#ASSERT `Art 13(11)(a) the payment is inconsistent with the statement` `the interpretation with any statement provided` (`Payment by the charity` WITH description IS "a fee", `date of the payment` IS YMD 2026 5 1, `statements provided` IS LIST (`Statement of intentions as to payments` OF (YMD 2024 1 1), TRUE), (`Statement of intentions as to payments` OF (YMD 2025 1 1), FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(11)(a) the payment is inconsistent with the statement` `ind-b5 A` (`Payment by the charity` WITH description IS "a fee", `date of the payment` IS YMD 2026 5 1, `statements provided` IS LIST (`Statement of intentions as to payments` OF (YMD 2024 1 1), TRUE), (`Statement of intentions as to payments` OF (YMD 2025 1 1), FALSE))

§ `Reading checks for G5 added at review (F5.1 B/C, F5.10 B, F5.2 B/C, F5.11 B, F5.3 B, F5.5 B, F5.9 B, F5.13 B)`

-- F5.1 B (10 days from the event, F5.10 A): last prompt day 2026-03-11.
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the report was made promptly` (`the interpretation with promptness measured from the event in` 10) `ind-b5 timing with late awareness` (`ind-b5 a report made on` (YMD 2026 3 11))
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the report was made promptly` (`the interpretation with promptness measured from the event in` 10) `ind-b5 timing with late awareness` (`ind-b5 a report made on` (YMD 2026 3 12))
-- F5.1 C (10 days from awareness): a report on 2026-03-12 is prompt.
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the report was made promptly` (`the interpretation with promptness measured from awareness in` 10) `ind-b5 timing with late awareness` (`ind-b5 a report made on` (YMD 2026 3 12))
-- F5.10 B (the day of the event counted as day one, with F5.1 B): the last prompt day is 2026-03-10.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the report was made promptly` (`the interpretation with promptness from the event in` 10) `ind-b5 timing with late awareness` (`ind-b5 a report made on` (YMD 2026 3 11))
-- F5.1 A (taken): the input judgement decides (here, not prompt).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the report was made promptly` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 timing with late awareness` (`ind-b5 a report made on` (YMD 2026 3 2))
-- F5.2 A (taken, the calendar year), B (a financial year ending 31 March) and C (from each anniversary of registration on 2019-01-10), for 2026-06-01.
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `ind-b5 A` `ind-b5 a general-section company charity` NOTHING (YMD 2026 6 1) EQUALS (`Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2026 1 1), (YMD 2026 12 31))
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the charity's own financial year` `ind-b5 a general-section company charity` (JUST (`Day on which a financial year ends` OF 3, 31)) (YMD 2026 6 1) EQUALS (`Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2026 4 1), (YMD 2027 3 31))
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the year from each anniversary of registration` `ind-b5 a general-section company charity` NOTHING (YMD 2026 6 1) EQUALS (`Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2026 1 10), (YMD 2027 1 9))
-- F5.11 A (clamp) and B (roll), with F5.2 C: registered 2020-02-29, the year containing 2021-03-01 begins on 2021-02-28 or 2021-03-01.
#ASSERT (`Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the year from each anniversary of registration` `ind-b5 a charity registered on 29 February 2020` NOTHING (YMD 2021 3 1))'s `first day` EQUALS YMD 2021 2 28
#ASSERT (`Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the year from each anniversary of registration and 29 February rolled` `ind-b5 a charity registered on 29 February 2020` NOTHING (YMD 2021 3 1))'s `first day` EQUALS YMD 2021 3 1
-- F5.3 A (taken) and B: a relief Order naming "an Order under paragraph (8)" reaches an Order under (7) made by virtue of (8) on A, nothing on B.
#ASSERT `Art 13(10) the effect of the relief Order on the provision` `ind-b5 A` (`ind-b5 relief order` TRUE TRUE `a provision of an Order under paragraph (8)`) `a provision of an Order under paragraph (7) made by virtue of paragraph (8)` EQUALS `the provision does not apply to the charity`
#ASSERT `Art 13(10) the effect of the relief Order on the provision` `the interpretation with no Order under paragraph (8)` (`ind-b5 relief order` TRUE TRUE `a provision of an Order under paragraph (8)`) `a provision of an Order under paragraph (7) made by virtue of paragraph (8)` EQUALS `the provision applies in full`
-- F5.5 A (taken) and B: a return sent on the due date is not late on A, late on B.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(8) the annual return is late` `ind-b5 A` (`Order under Article 13(7) and (8)` OF (JUST (YMD 2026 6 30)), NOTHING) (YMD 2026 6 30)
#ASSERT `Art 13(8) the annual return is late` `the interpretation with a return due before the due date` (`Order under Article 13(7) and (8)` OF (JUST (YMD 2026 6 30)), NOTHING) (YMD 2026 6 30)
-- F5.5: with no Order fixing a due date, lateness is not answered.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 13(8) the annual return is late` `ind-b5 A` (`Order under Article 13(7) and (8)` OF NOTHING, NOTHING) (YMD 2026 6 30)
-- F5.9 A (taken) and B: a 10-day order from 2026-01-01 runs 1 to 10 January on A, 2 to 11 January on B.
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is in operation on the day` `ind-b5 A` (`a specified period` (YMD 2026 1 1) 10) (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(3) the order is in operation on the day` `ind-b5 A` (`a specified period` (YMD 2026 1 1) 10) (YMD 2026 1 11)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(3) the order is in operation on the day` `the interpretation with the court period starting the day after` (`a specified period` (YMD 2026 1 1) 10) (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is in operation on the day` `the interpretation with the court period starting the day after` (`a specified period` (YMD 2026 1 1) 10) (YMD 2026 1 11)
-- F5.13 A (taken) and B: an event of 2025-12-20 learned of on 2026-01-05 arises in 2025 on A, in 2026 on B.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(7) the matter arose during the year to which the return relates` `ind-b5 A` (`Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2026 1 1), (YMD 2026 12 31)) (`Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH `date of the event or proposal` IS YMD 2025 12 20, `date the charity became aware of the matter` IS YMD 2026 1 5)
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the matter arose during the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the date of awareness` (`Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2026 1 1), (YMD 2026 12 31)) (`Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH `date of the event or proposal` IS YMD 2025 12 20, `date the charity became aware of the matter` IS YMD 2026 1 5)
